       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"File Upload Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a file upload form?\", \"a\": \"A file upload form is a web form with at least one field that takes a file, such as a photo, a resume, or a signed document, alongside the typed answers. Each file stays tied to the submission it arrived with, and whoever reviews it can see who sent it and why.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a file upload form?\", \"a\": \"Describe it to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in plain English: each upload field, the types it accepts, and what should happen to the file after submit. It builds the form and the database behind it. The free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a file upload form template include?\", \"a\": \"Start with the sender's name and email, then one upload field per file you need, each with a one-line note on what the file should show. Close with a confirmation screen that lists every file received by name. A file upload form template from a gallery gives you those fields; how files are named and who gets each one are still yours to add.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a free file upload form split uploads across several steps?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/multi-step'>multi step form</a> can put each group of files on its own screen, such as identity documents on one and room photos on the next. People then see a short list at each step. Emergent is free to start, and that plan covers building and publishing a free file upload form like this one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What file types should a file upload form accept?\", \"a\": \"Accept only the types the person opening the file can use, and set them field by field. A photo field might take JPG and PNG, while a signed agreement takes PDF alone. A field open to every type eventually receives a file nobody on the team can open.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a file upload form work in HTML?\", \"a\": \"It is a form element containing an input with type=file. MDN's guidance is to set the form's encoding to multipart/form-data whenever it contains an input with type=file. Code on your server then has to receive each file, check it, and save it with the rest of the submission.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I put a file upload form on a landing page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The form can sit in a section of the page or open from a button. For a contest or a casting call, an animated landing page can show last year's winning entries above the upload form. An app built with Emergent keeps every entry that arrives, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a file upload form take files from people who have no account?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the form is built as its own app: it can take files with no sign-in, or ask for one when you need to know exactly who sent each file. Other tools set their own rule. In Google Forms, responders need to sign in to a Google Account to answer a file upload question. Uploaded files are stored in a new folder in the form owner's Google Drive.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I keep files from a file upload form organized?\", \"a\": \"Give each file a name that starts with the submission number, and file it in one folder per client instead of one long list. If you run several file upload forms, add a short code for each form, such as LSE for leases, to the front of every name. An app built with Emergent can also copy each file to any storage tool with an API.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can people upload photos from a phone camera to a file upload form?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the upload field accepts images. In HTML, the capture attribute specifies which camera to use for capturing an image or video on a phone. To get people to the form from a poster or a counter sign, a qr code landing page can open it in one scan.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
